    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, read from the YAML pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`), its function classes, the DTO constraints, and the escalation handlers.\n\n## Before the pipeline\n\n1. **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`): `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 else `AuthorizationDeniedException` (403).\n2. **Bean validation of the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`, runs before `BuildOwner`'s body). Any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` (400):\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, `@Size 1\u201330`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`, `@Size 1\u201330`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u2013255`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u201380`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$` (optional)\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size 1\u201320`\n   - `email`: `@Size max 255`\n   - `registrationDate`: `@Valid`\n\nEvery pipeline step below runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so it is one transaction committed at the end.\n\n## `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner` (validations + side-effects)\n\n3. Normalize the address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE` \u2192 `STREET/ROAD/AVENUE`).\n4. **Required-field check**: `firstName`, `lastName`, address (must be non-empty *after* normalization), `city`, `telephone` \u2014 any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **Normalize telephone** to E.164 (strip separators, default country code +61, drop a leading 0, enforce 8\u201315 digits and per-country national length) \u2014 invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400). *Side-effect:* stores canonical telephone on the request.\n6. Store the normalized address back on the request.\n7. **Normalize email**: blank \u2192 null; otherwise syntactic regex check \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400) if malformed; stored trimmed + lower-cased.\n8. Map request \u2192 `Owner` (via `OwnerMapper`).\n9. *Side-effect:* set **registrationDate** \u2014 default to today if absent, then roll a Saturday/Sunday forward to the next Monday (business-day adjustment).\n10. *Side-effect:* set **customerCode** = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is 1 + count of existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive).\n11. Publish the built `Owner` and the `sharesHousehold` flag.\n\n## `checkPostcode` \u2014 `CheckOwnerPostcode`\n\n12. If postcode present: re-check 4-digit format, then check it falls in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region \u2192 any 4 digits allowed) \u2014 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Absent = no-op.\n\n## `assignHousehold` \u2014 `AssignOwnerHousehold`\n\n13. *Side-effect:* set `householdSize = 1`.\n14. If `sharesHousehold` is true and existing owners match on normalized last name + address: *side-effects* \u2014 stamp a shared stable `householdId` and the new `householdSize` on the new owner **and on every existing member**, and **save each existing member** (mutating other records). No duplicate rejection here.\n\n## `checkIdentity` \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`\n\n15. Reject if the derived identity key (`E.164 telephone | email | householdId`) equals an existing owner's whole key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## `checkCityCapacity` \u2014 `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n\n16. Reject if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n## `checkDailyLimit` \u2014 `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\n\n17. Reject if \u2265 100 owners already exist on the (adjusted) registrationDate \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n## `checkBulkSignup` \u2014 `CheckOwnerBulkSignup`\n\n18. *Side-effect:* set `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already exist on that registrationDate.\n\n## `countNamesakes` \u2014 `CountOwnerNamesakes`\n\n19. *Side-effect:* set `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first + last name (case-insensitive).\n\n## `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`\n\n20. *Side-effect:* persist the owner (assigns its id).\n\n## `audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`\n\n21. *Side-effect:* write an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel (1\u20133, from email presence + zero namesakes).\n\n## `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`\n\n22. Send **201 Created**, `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, body = `OwnerDto`.\n\n**Notes:** No `@RequestBody` is bound after step `build` (single-read rule). Validation ordering is deliberate \u2014 body/bean validation and field/format checks (400s) precede the not-found/conflict/limit semantic checks (409/429). Membership level is computed only for the audit log, not stored."
